DOCX ends a table of contents at the next paragraph's start

Word ends a TOC field at the start of the paragraph after the last
entry: alone in an empty paragraph, or before the text that follows it.
The import keeps that paragraph inside the index only for a titled TOC
whose end stands alone; otherwise the paragraph lands after the index
section (untitled and bare TOCs, R15.11c; text or a shape after the
end, patch 0078). The export then closed the field inside the last
entry, and Word's Update Table left an extra empty line after the
entries (Ely R15.11k).

The import now marks that paragraph with "TOCFieldEnd" in its grab
bag. When a table of contents' last paragraph is not empty and the
paragraph right after its section carries the mark, DOCX closes the
field at the start of that paragraph and keeps the paragraph inside
the TOC content control. Unmarked paragraphs, such as the body text
after a TOC made in Writer, keep the old export: a shape-based guess
would pull the user's heading into the field, and Word's "Remove Table
of Contents" would delete it. Other indexes keep the old export too.
testFdo77129 now expects the end paragraph inside the control, so the
body has one paragraph fewer outside it.

